<p>Everyone who uses HardPoint gets their own login, so the activity log shows who did what. Invite people from
  <strong>Settings › Staff</strong>: they get an email to set their password (the link in it works for 3 days). Give each person the
  role that fits their job.</p>

<h2>Roles</h2>
<ul>
  <li><strong>Owner</strong>: everything, including billing, exporting data and closing the account.</li>
  <li><strong>Manager</strong>: runs the shop: products and prices, stock, purchasing, customers, reports, and approving discounts, voids and returns.</li>
  <li><strong>Cashier</strong>: sells, takes payments and does returns at the till (with approval where needed).</li>
  <li><strong>Stock clerk</strong>: receives deliveries, orders from suppliers, moves stock between branches and counts it.</li>
  <li><strong>Accountant</strong>: the money side without the till: customer accounts and statements, supplier invoices and payments, and reports.</li>
</ul>
<p>Each person only sees the areas their role uses: a cashier sees Home, Sell, Customers and Stock, and starts at the till.</p>
<p>Managers can add staff and change their roles, but only an owner can make someone an owner, or change or remove an owner.
  Removing someone signs them out of every till and phone straight away.</p>

