<h2>Quick switching with a PIN</h2>
<p>On a shared till, cashiers and stock clerks don't need to sign out. Each sets a 4 to 6 digit PIN under <strong>My profile</strong>
  (open your name in the top right). Then <strong>Switch user</strong>, in the same menu, changes who's selling in a couple of taps. Five
  wrong tries lock the PIN until its owner signs in with their password and sets a new one.</p>

<h2>Discounts and other things that need approval</h2>
<p>Cashiers can give discounts up to the limit set in <strong>Settings › Shop details</strong> (5% to begin with). Anything bigger, voids,
  returns and going over a customer's credit limit ask for an owner's or manager's <strong>approval PIN</strong> at the till. Owners and
  managers set theirs under <strong>My profile › Approval PIN</strong>. It authorises that one action only and signs nobody in; who
  approved it is recorded. After 10 wrong approval PINs in 15 minutes the shop accepts none for a while, so a PIN can't be guessed;
  an owner or manager can still approve by signing in at the till themselves.</p>

<h2>Two-factor sign-in</h2>
<p>Owners and managers should turn on two-factor sign-in under <strong>My profile</strong>, using an authenticator app, and keep the
  recovery codes somewhere safe. The owner can require it for all owners and managers in <strong>Settings › Shop details</strong>.</p>
<p>If someone has lost their phone and their recovery codes, the owner opens them in <strong>Settings › Staff</strong>, types their own
  password under <strong>Two-factor sign-in</strong> and presses <strong>Reset two-factor</strong>. That person is signed out everywhere,
  emailed, and sets two-factor up again with their password. The reset is in <strong>Settings › Activity</strong>. Someone who also works
  for another shop, or an owner with no other owner, is reset by HardPoint support instead, after we've checked who they are.</p>

<h2>Seeing who did what</h2>
<p><strong>Settings › Activity</strong> lists every change: prices, stock adjustments, voids, approvals, settings. It can't be edited.</p>
